Z||000006||drednot||08-25-2001||04:59 PM||||it is an 85 4cyl 5 speed.  I am not taking the thing apart again.  It may be time to junk it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||08-25-2001||05:14 PM||||Did you check to make sure that the clutch arm(the thing that the slave pushes against) isn't slipping on the shaft that goes into the tranny? Just had another thought- I once thought that I had the same problem, I couldn't get the clutch to fully disengage. As it turned out I had (believe it or not ) too much clutch throw. The TO bearing was pushing the disk up against the flywheel. Just for giggles and grins try pushing the clutch pedal about half way and see if that makes a difference.<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rodrv6||08-25-2001||11:21 PM||||You might want to check the release arm that the slave cylinder pushrod fits into.  If it is an early design made from bent flat steel then it may be cracked down where it attatches to the pivot on the transmission.  Too much flex here = insufficient travel at the throwout bearing.  The later design is a cast or forged piece that is nearly bulletproof.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000009||EdsB52||08-26-2001||01:14 AM||||How did you bleed the master cyl, lines, and slave cylinder? Air can get trapped in the master, try bleeding it at the line-nut that goes into the m. cylinder. Are you sure the clutch ledal you got was the steel one? Go under your dash and ensure the "L-bracket" that retains the stud that pushes the master cylinder rod is 90 degrees. If not, get a crescent wrench or something and bend it forward a bit. Make sure the carpet and floor mats aren't limiting your travel either.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ROB MAC||08-26-2001||09:20 AM||||My slave seal is shot. Does not leak out but lets air in. I am losing a fraction of an inch of travel causing problem. I remove the bleeder screw, pull back the pushrod, squirt the air out and it's fine for a day or two. New seal on the way. ||||reg||1
